@chapter Description
@c man begin DESCRIPTION

This document describes some generic features and utilities provided
by the libavutil library.

@c man end DESCRIPTION

@anchor{Stream metadata}
@chapter Stream metadata
@c man begin STREAM METADATA

Some stream metadata tags are understood by the transcoder when a subtitle
stream is rendered onto a video canvas.  The @code{3d-plane} tag, and the
language-specific form @code{3d-plane-@var{lang}} where @var{lang} is the
language tag of the stream, name the index of an OFMD subtitle-depth sequence
for multiview video.  The value must be an integer in the range @code{0..31},
with only blanks or horizontal tabs permitted before or after it.

A language-specific tag takes precedence over the bare tag.  If both forms
are present, the language-specific value is used; if that value is malformed,
it shadows the bare tag and no plane is advertised.  If neither tag is
present, or the effective value is malformed, no plane is advertised and the
subtitle is rendered flat.

@c man end STREAM METADATA

